# =============================================================================
# 10-base.list.chroot - NimbusOS base system
# =============================================================================
# What: system basics, networking, audio, firmware, CPU microcode and Mesa.
# Why:  spec section 1 (Apps row) plus what a desktop needs underneath it.
#       The kernel is added by live-build itself (lb config --linux-flavours).
#
# Format rules for every list in this directory (live-build 1:20250505 passes
# the file through printf and runs lines that start with an exclamation mark):
#   * one package name per line, plain comment lines starting with a hash;
#   * no comment after a package name, no percent sign, no backslash.
# tools/verify-trixie.sh enforces these rules and proves every package exists
# in Trixie. Unless a list is marked otherwise, its packages are also Depends
# of nimbusos-desktop (tools/gen-desktop-depends.sh), so adding a package here
# also delivers it to installed systems with their next update.
# =============================================================================

# System basics
sudo
locales
console-setup
keyboard-configuration
bash-completion
man-db
less
nano
ca-certificates
curl
gpg
cryptsetup
systemd-timesyncd
unattended-upgrades

# Networking
network-manager
openssh-client

# Audio and Bluetooth (PipeWire with WirePlumber)
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber
libspa-0.2-bluetooth
bluez

# Firmware, from non-free-firmware. firmware-intel-graphics carries the
# Intel GPU firmware that Trixie split out of firmware-misc-nonfree.
firmware-linux
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-sof-signed

# CPU microcode, from non-free-firmware
intel-microcode
amd64-microcode

# Graphics: Mesa OpenGL, Vulkan and VA-API drivers
libgl1-mesa-dri
mesa-vulkan-drivers
mesa-va-drivers

# Flatpak (the Flathub remote is added by nimbusos-release)
flatpak

# Boot splash (the theme ships in nimbusos-branding)
plymouth
